<title>USA: PHLX to halve SuperCap index from March 24.</title>
<headline>PHLX to halve SuperCap index from March 24.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philadelphia Stock Exchange (PHLX) said it had received U.S. Securities and Exchange Commisssion approval to split its SuperCap Index HFX2 in half.</p>
<p>It said the split will be effective from the start of trading Monday, March 24.</p>
<p>In late morning trading Friday, the index was up 0.48 at 542.83.</p>
<p>The split means strike prices will be halved and outstanding positions will be doubled, the PHLX said.  </p>
<p>Currently HFX2 April options have strikes of 500, 510, 550, 560, 570, 580 and 590.</p>
<p>May options have strikes of 550, 560, 570, 580, 590, 600 and 610. In the June series, strikes include 480, 485, 490, 550, 560, 570, 580, 590 and 600.</p>
<p>The HFX2 September series has strikes of 455, 480, 505, 530, 540, 560 and 570.</p>
<p>The SuperCap index comprises AT&amp;T, Coca-Cola Co, Exxon Corp, General Electric Co and Philip Morris Cos Inc.</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
